<title>PANAMA: IADB loans $56 mln for two Panama highways.</title>
<headline>IADB loans $56 mln for two Panama highways.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican company Proyectos y Construcciones (PYCSA) will obtain a $56-million loan from the Inter-American Development Bank (IADB) to complete two highways in Panama, an IADB spokeswoman said Thursday.</p>
<p>Terms and conditions of the loan were not immediately available and she said: &quot;We still have to work out various conditions and documents. They should be getting the money in the next few days.&quot;</p>
<p>PYCSA will use the funds to complete the Corredor Norte and Panama-Colon highways, two major thoroughfares in the small Central American nation which will ease traffic around the capital city and the Atlantic coast city of Colon, the country's second-largest city.</p>
<p>((-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739))</p>
